en.prompt:
A colleague wrote the module below. It should take arst_n, an active-low reset from a board pin that is asynchronous to clk. It should produce srst_n, an active-low reset for the core. srst_n must assert immediately when arst_n goes low, even if clk is not running. It must be released only after passing through two flip-flops clocked by clk.

```verilog
module rst_sync (
  input  wire clk,
  input  wire arst_n,
  output wire srst_n
);
  reg q1, q2;
  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (!arst_n) begin
      q1 <= 1'b1;
      q2 <= 1'b1;
    end else begin
      q1 <= 1'b1;
      q2 <= q1;
    end
  end
  assign srst_n = q1;
endmodule
```

The module contains exactly three bugs. Find each one, explain what goes wrong in hardware because of it, and write the corrected module.

en.reference_solution:
Bug 1: the sensitivity list is `always @(posedge clk)` and is missing `or negedge arst_n`. The reset is therefore synchronous. If the PLL has not locked or clk is gated at power-up, the core never enters reset. The specification requires immediate assertion. In addition, the raw asynchronous arst_n now feeds the D-side logic of q2 as well as q1. When it is released near an edge, q2 itself can go metastable, so the synchronizer protects nothing.

Bug 2: q1 and q2 are reset to 1'b1. srst_n is active-low, so during reset the output reads 1, which means "not in reset". The core is never reset. Both flops must reset to 1'b0.

Bug 3: `assign srst_n = q1;` takes the output from the first stage. q1 is the flop whose asynchronous clear is released asynchronously, so it is the one that can go metastable when arst_n rises near a clock edge. q2 gives it a full clock cycle to resolve, so the output must be q2.

Corrected module:
```verilog
module rst_sync (
  input  wire clk,
  input  wire arst_n,
  output wire srst_n
);
  reg q1, q2;
  always @(posedge clk or negedge arst_n) begin
    if (!arst_n) begin
      q1 <= 1'b0;
      q2 <= 1'b0;
    end else begin
      q1 <= 1'b1;
      q2 <= q1;
    end
  end
  assign srst_n = q2;
endmodule
```
Behaviour: arst_n falls, so q1 = q2 = 0 at once and srst_n = 0 with no clock. arst_n rises, q1 becomes 1 on the next edge, q2 becomes 1 one edge later, and srst_n is released synchronously to clk.

