```verilog
module watchdog #(
  parameter LIMIT = 1000
) (
  input  wire clk,
  input  wire rst_n,
  input  wire start,
  input  wire kick,
  output wire active,
  output wire fired
);
  localparam W = $clog2(LIMIT);
  localparam [W-1:0] RELOAD = LIMIT - 1;
  localparam IDLE = 1'b0, RUN = 1'b1;

  reg         state_q, state_d;
  reg [W-1:0] cnt_q,   cnt_d;
  reg         fired_q, fired_d;

  // registers only
  always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin
    if (!rst_n) begin
      state_q <= IDLE;
      cnt_q   <= {W{1'b0}};
      fired_q <= 1'b0;
    end else begin
      state_q <= state_d;
      cnt_q   <= cnt_d;
      fired_q <= fired_d;
    end
  end

  // next-state logic
  always @* begin
    state_d = state_q;   // defaults: hold, no pulse
    cnt_d   = cnt_q;
    fired_d = 1'b0;
    case (state_q)
      IDLE: if (start) begin
              state_d = RUN;
              cnt_d   = RELOAD;
            end
      RUN:  if (kick) begin
              cnt_d = RELOAD;               // kick has top priority
            end else if (cnt_q == {W{1'b0}}) begin
              state_d = IDLE;               // expiry
              fired_d = 1'b1;
            end else begin
              cnt_d = cnt_q - 1'b1;
            end
      default: state_d = IDLE;
    endcase
  end

  assign active = (state_q == RUN);
  assign fired  = fired_q;
endmodule
```

Edge count for LIMIT = 1000:
- W = $clog2(1000) = 10 bits, and RELOAD = 999 fits because 999 < 1024.
- After edge 0 the counter is 999 and the state is RUN.
- Edges 1 to 999 each decrement once, so after edge 999 the counter is 0.
- On edge 1000 the logic sees RUN, counter 0 and no kick. It goes to IDLE and fired_q becomes 1.
- So fired first becomes 1 immediately after edge 1000, which is LIMIT edges after the start edge. It stays 1 until edge 1001. In that same cycle active is already 0.

Synthesized hardware:
- 10 counter flip-flops, 1 state flip-flop and 1 fired flip-flop, all with asynchronous clear. That is W+2 = 12 flip-flops.
- A 10-bit compare-to-zero (a NOR reduction).
- A 10-bit decrementer.
- A MUX in front of each counter bit that selects among RELOAD, cnt_q-1 and cnt_q.
- Small gates for state_d and fired_d.
- No latches, because every combinational output has a default assignment.

